NOTE_ZH = "教材程度：大學三年級（undergrad）。依講義 lec05-kp08 以 view-from-text-v3 製作：先規劃頁面，每頁以一張原生資訊圖（HTML 設計後轉成原生節點）為主，名詞在同一頁圖內定義。共 10 頁，本單元為自主學習，課堂不講授；所有數字皆由程式計算。"
NOTE_EN = "Level: undergraduate (year 3). Made from the lecture lec05-kp08 with view-from-text-v3: pages were planned first and each page is mainly one native infographic (designed in HTML and converted to native nodes), with the terms defined on the same page. 10 pages; this unit is self-study and is not taught in class; every number is computed by program."
def fig(n, alt_zh, alt_en):
    return lambda: native(f"kp08_p{n}", f"lec05-kp08-p{n}", KP.W, KP.H, JD, alt_en if os.environ.get("KP_LANG") == "en" else alt_zh)
P = []
NXT = {1: ("為什麼來回擺", "why the path zigzags"), 2: ("動量項", "the momentum term"), 3: ("動量為什麼有效", "why momentum works"), 4: ("兩條軌跡的比較", "the comparison of two paths"), 5: ("α 的最佳值", "the best value of α"), 6: ("自適應學習率", "the adaptive learning rate"), 7: ("quickprop", "quickprop"), 8: ("五種做法與牛頓法", "the five methods and Newton's method"), 9: ("小練習", "the exercises")}
PREV = {2: ("狹長谷底", "the narrow valley"), 3: ("為什麼來回擺", "why the path zigzags"), 4: ("動量項", "the momentum term"), 5: ("動量為什麼有效", "why momentum works"), 6: ("兩條軌跡的比較", "the comparison of two paths"), 7: ("α 的最佳值", "the best value of α"), 8: ("自適應學習率", "the adaptive learning rate"), 9: ("quickprop", "quickprop"), 10: ("五種做法與牛頓法", "the five methods and Newton's method")}
def add(n, lab, title, bridge, notes, alt):
    zh, en = notes
    if n in PREV: zh = f"承接上一頁的「{PREV[n][0]}」。" + zh; en = f"Following the previous page on {PREV[n][1]}. " + en
    if n == 10: zh += "到這裡這個單元就結束了；之後請接著讀下一單元。"; en += " That ends this unit; next, move on to the next unit."
    if n in NXT: zh += f"接下來的下一頁是「{NXT[n][0]}」。"; en += f" Next, the next page covers {NXT[n][1]}."
    P.append(dict(lab=lab, title=title, bridge=bridge, notes=(zh, en), layout="freeform", spec=fig(n, *alt)))
add(1, ("狹長谷底", "Narrow valley"),
    ("狹長谷底讓普通梯度下降走 100 步才到 |w| < 0.001，軌跡在 w₂ 方向上下擺", "In a narrow valley plain descent needs 100 steps and swings up and down along w₂"),
    ("KP07 的訓練動輒上千個 epoch，原因之一是梯度下降本身慢。慢在哪裡？", "KP07 training takes thousands of epochs, partly because gradient descent itself is slow. Where does the slowness come from?"),
    ("這是 KP08 的第一頁，這個單元是自主學習。先備三件事：梯度下降（KP06、KP07），每一步往梯度反方向走，步子是學習率 μ 乘梯度；等高線，把代價相同的點連起來，越密代價變化越快；二次函數的圖是碗形。曲率是代價面彎得多厲害；狹長谷底（病態代價面）是一個方向曲率很大、另一個很小，等高線是很扁的橢圓。例子是本講義自行設計的 J 等於二分之一乘 w1 平方加 20 乘 w2 平方，w2 方向曲率 20、w1 方向曲率 1，起點 (−4, 1)，μ 等於 0.08。普通梯度下降走 100 步才到 |w| 小於 0.001，軌跡在 w2 方向上下擺（程式計算）。",
     "This is the first page of KP08, a self-study unit. Prerequisites: gradient descent (KP06, KP07), where each step goes against the gradient by the learning rate mu times the gradient; contour lines, which join points of equal cost and are denser where the cost changes faster; and the bowl shape of a quadratic. Curvature is how sharply the cost surface bends; a narrow valley (an ill-conditioned surface) has a very large curvature in one direction and a very small one in the other, so the contours are flat ellipses. The example is designed for this lecture: J equals one half of w1 squared plus 20 w2 squared, curvature 20 along w2 and 1 along w1, start (-4, 1), mu equal to 0.08. Plain gradient descent needs 100 steps to reach |w| below 0.001, and the path swings up and down along w2 (computed by program)."),
    ("Contours of J = 1/2(w1^2 + 20 w2^2) as flat ellipses and the red plain gradient-descent path from (-4, 1) to the origin in 100 steps, swinging up and down along w2.",) * 2)
add(2, ("為什麼來回擺", "Why it zigzags"),
    ("w₂ 每步變號、只縮到 0.6 倍，w₁ 每步只縮 8%：μ 要小於 0.1 才穩，卻讓 w₁ 走得慢", "w₂ flips sign and shrinks 0.6 times per step, w₁ only 8%: μ < 0.1 is stable but slow"),
    ("狹長谷底讓普通梯度下降走 100 步，軌跡在 w₂ 方向上下擺。軌跡為什麼會來回擺？", "In the narrow valley plain descent needs 100 steps and swings up and down along w₂. Why does the path zigzag?"),
    ("這一頁拆開兩個方向。陡的方向 w2 的梯度是 20 乘 w2，更新 w2 減 0.08 乘 20 乘 w2 等於 負 0.6 乘 w2，每步變號、只縮到 0.6 倍：1、負 0.6、0.36、負 0.216。平的方向 w1 更新成 0.92 乘 w1，同方向、每步只縮 8%。兩難在於 μ 要小於 2 除以 20 等於 0.1，w2 才不會越擺越大；μ 等於 0.12 時因子是 1 減 2.4 等於 負 1.4，60 步後 |w| 已達 5.86 乘 10 的 8 次方（程式計算）。但這麼小的步長讓 w1 走得慢。",
     "This page separates the two directions. In the steep direction the gradient of w2 is 20 w2, so the update w2 minus 0.08 times 20 times w2 equals minus 0.6 w2: the sign flips every step and the value shrinks only to 0.6 times, 1, minus 0.6, 0.36, minus 0.216. In the flat direction w1 becomes 0.92 w1, the same direction and only 8% smaller per step. The dilemma is that mu must stay below 2 over 20, which is 0.1, so that w2 does not swing wider; with mu equal to 0.12 the factor is 1 minus 2.4, equal to minus 1.4, and after 60 steps |w| has reached 5.86 times 10 to the 8 (computed by program). But so small a step makes w1 crawl."),
    ("Left: w2 values 1, -0.6, 0.36, -0.216 swing around zero (factor -0.6). Right: w1 values -4, -3.68, -3.386 creep to zero (factor 0.92). Below: mu must be below 2/20 = 0.1; mu = 0.12 gives factor -1.4 and |w| = 5.86e8 after 60 steps.",) * 2)
add(3, ("動量項", "Momentum term"),
    ("動量 Δw(t) = αΔw(t−1) − μg(t)：第 2 步 w₂ 的慣性 −0.96 與梯度 +0.96 剛好抵銷", "Momentum Δw(t) = αΔw(t−1) − μg(t): at step 2 the w₂ inertia −0.96 and gradient +0.96 cancel"),
    ("w₂ 每步變號、只縮到 0.6 倍，w₁ 每步只縮 8%，μ 又不能大於 0.1。能不能讓 w₁ 走快、w₂ 不擺？", "w₂ flips sign and shrinks 0.6 times per step, w₁ only 8%, and μ must stay below 0.1. Can w₁ go faster while w₂ stops swinging?"),
    ("這一頁定義動量。動量讓更新帶著慣性：這一步除了本次的梯度步，還加上上一步的 α 倍，Δw(t) 等於 α 乘 Δw(t 減 1) 減 μ 乘 g(t)；α 叫動量因子，實務上取 0.1 到 0.8，α 等於 0 就是普通梯度下降。手算 μ 等於 0.08、α 等於 0.6、起點 (−4, 1)：第 1 步更新量 (0.32, 負 1.6)，w 等於 (負 3.68, 負 0.6)；第 2 步 0.6 乘 (0.32, 負 1.6) 減 0.08 乘 (負 3.68, 負 12) 等於 (0.4864, 0)，w2 的慣性負 0.96 與梯度 0.96 剛好抵銷；第 3 步 (0.5473, 0.96)，w 等於 (負 2.646, 0.36)。",
     "This page defines momentum. Momentum lets the update carry inertia: besides this gradient step it adds alpha times the previous update, so delta w at t equals alpha times delta w at t minus 1 minus mu times g at t; alpha is the momentum factor, 0.1 to 0.8 in practice, and alpha equal to 0 is plain gradient descent. By hand with mu equal to 0.08, alpha equal to 0.6 and start (-4, 1): step 1 gives the update (0.32, minus 1.6) and w equal to (minus 3.68, minus 0.6); step 2 is 0.6 times (0.32, minus 1.6) minus 0.08 times (minus 3.68, minus 12), equal to (0.4864, 0), where the w2 inertia of minus 0.96 and the gradient part of 0.96 cancel exactly; step 3 gives (0.5473, 0.96) and w equal to (minus 2.646, 0.36)."),
    ("Momentum formula and a table of the first three steps (mu=0.08, alpha=0.6): updates (0.32,-1.6), (0.4864,0), (0.5473,0.96) and w (-3.68,-0.6), (-3.194,-0.6), (-2.646,0.36); at step 2 the w2 inertia -0.96 and gradient +0.96 cancel.",) * 2)
add(4, ("為什麼有效", "Why it works"),
    ("動量是歷史梯度的指數加權平均：平的方向總權重放大 1/(1−α) 倍，陡的方向正負抵消", "Momentum averages past gradients: gain 1/(1−α) where flat, cancellation where steep"),
    ("動量 Δw(t) = αΔw(t−1) − μg(t)，第 2 步 w₂ 的慣性與梯度剛好抵銷。這個式子為什麼有效？", "Momentum Δw(t) = αΔw(t−1) − μg(t): at step 2 the w₂ inertia −0.96 and gradient +0.96 cancel. Why does this formula work?"),
    ("這一頁展開動量式。指數加權平均是最近的梯度權重最大，越久以前的每回合再乘 α 變小，權重是 1、α、α 平方、…。展開 T 步，Δw(T) 等於 負 μ 乘 α 的 t 次方乘 g(T 減 t) 的總和，加上 α 的 T 次方乘 Δw(0)，最後一項幾步就趨近 0。梯度不變（平的方向）時總權重 1 加 α 加 α 平方 … 等於 1 除以 (1 減 α)：α 等於 0.6 是 2.5 倍，α 等於 0.8 是 5 倍（固定梯度跑 80 步驗證，程式計算）。梯度正負交替（陡的方向）時，權重正負交替，加權平均互相抵消。",
     "This page expands the momentum formula. An exponentially weighted average gives the latest gradient the largest weight and multiplies older ones by alpha at every step back, so the weights are 1, alpha, alpha squared, and so on. Expanding T steps, delta w at T equals minus mu times the sum of alpha to the t times g at T minus t, plus alpha to the T times delta w at 0, and the last term vanishes within a few steps. With a constant gradient (the flat direction) the total weight 1 plus alpha plus alpha squared and so on equals 1 over 1 minus alpha: 2.5 times for alpha 0.6 and 5 times for alpha 0.8 (verified by 80 steps with a fixed gradient, computed by program). With alternating gradients (the steep direction) the weights alternate in sign and the average cancels."),
    ("Bars of the weights alpha^t for t = 0..5 with alpha 0.6 and 0.8; a fixed gradient gives total weight 1/(1-alpha) = 2.5 and 5; alternating gradients cancel.",) * 2)
add(5, ("兩條軌跡", "Two paths"),
    ("同起點同 μ = 0.08：普通梯度下降 100 步，α = 0.6 的動量只要 28 步", "Same start and μ: plain descent needs 100 steps, momentum with α = 0.6 only 28"),
    ("動量把平的方向的總權重放大 1/(1−α) 倍、陡的方向正負抵消。和普通梯度下降比，軌跡差多少？", "Momentum gains 1/(1−α) where flat and cancels where steep. Compared with plain descent, how different are the paths?"),
    ("這一頁比較兩條軌跡。同起點 (−4, 1)、同 μ 等於 0.08：普通梯度下降 100 步到 |w| 小於 0.001，α 等於 0.6 的動量 28 步（程式計算），28 除以 100 等於 0.28，約快 3.6 倍。紅色軌跡在 w2 方向上下擺很多回，綠色的擺幅縮得更快，w1 方向也走得更快。代價是多存一份上一步的更新量，多一個旋鈕 α。",
     "This page compares the two paths. With the same start (-4, 1) and mu equal to 0.08, plain gradient descent needs 100 steps to reach |w| below 0.001 and momentum with alpha 0.6 needs 28 (computed by program); 28 over 100 is 0.28, about 3.6 times faster. The red path swings many times along w2 while the green swing shrinks faster and w1 also advances faster. The price is one more stored vector, the previous update, and one more knob, alpha."),
    ("Contours with the red plain path (100 steps) and the green momentum path (28 steps) from (-4, 1); bars 100 versus 28; the price is one stored vector and the knob alpha.",) * 2)
add(6, ("α 的最佳值", "Best α"),
    ("α 不是越大越好：α = 0.6 只要 28 步最快，α ≥ 0.9 反而比不用動量更慢", "A larger α is not better: α = 0.6 is fastest at 28 steps, α ≥ 0.9 is slower than none"),
    ("動量 α = 0.6 只要 28 步，普通梯度下降要 100 步。α 取多大最好？越大越快嗎？", "Momentum with α = 0.6 needs 28 steps against 100 for plain descent. Which α is best, and is a larger α always faster?"),
    ("這一頁破除迷思：α 越大越好。μ 等於 0.08 時所需步數（程式計算）：α 等於 0 是 100、0.3 是 65、0.5 是 36、0.6 是 28、0.7 是 44、0.8 是 63、0.9 是 137、0.95 是 247。α 大於等於 0.9 比不用動量更慢：慣性太大，在谷底衝過頭，像單擺晃很久才停。實務上常取 0.1 到 0.8，最佳值看問題，要試；來源報告過 2 倍以上的加速。",
     "This page dispels the myth that a larger alpha is always better. Steps needed at mu equal to 0.08 (computed by program): alpha 0 gives 100, 0.3 gives 65, 0.5 gives 36, 0.6 gives 28, 0.7 gives 44, 0.8 gives 63, 0.9 gives 137 and 0.95 gives 247. Alpha of 0.9 or more is slower than no momentum: the inertia is so large that it overshoots the valley floor and swings like a pendulum for a long time. In practice 0.1 to 0.8 is common; the best value depends on the problem and must be tried, and the source reports speed-ups of 2 times or more."),
    ("Steps against alpha: 100, 65, 36, 28 (minimum at alpha 0.6), 44, 63, 137, 247 for alpha 0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 0.95; alpha at least 0.9 is slower than plain descent.",) * 2)
add(7, ("自適應學習率", "Adaptive rate"),
    ("自適應學習率：變好 μ 乘 1.05、變壞乘 0.7，μ₀ = 0.02 時從 411 步降到 61 步", "Adaptive learning rate: ×1.05 when better, ×0.7 when worse; μ₀ = 0.02 falls from 411 to 61 steps"),
    ("α 取 0.6 最快，α ≥ 0.9 比不用動量更慢，要試才知道。能不能讓學習率 μ 自己調？", "A larger α is not better: α = 0.6 is fastest at 28 steps, α ≥ 0.9 is slower than none. Can the learning rate μ adjust itself?"),
    ("這一頁讓學習率自己調。自適應學習率看代價 J 的前後比值：比值小於 1（變好）μ 乘 1.05；比值大於 1.04（變壞）μ 乘 0.7，這一步不採用、動量歸零；其餘不變。不對稱：變好慢慢加，變壞大力煞車。結果（程式計算）：起始 μ0 等於 0.02，普通 411 步、自適應 61 步；μ0 等於 0.12 普通直接爆開，自適應共 95 步（其中 12 步被拒絕）仍收斂；μ0 等於 0.08 本來就接近最佳，100 步對 93 步，沒好多少。",
     "This page lets the learning rate adjust itself. The adaptive learning rate looks at the ratio of successive costs J: when the ratio is below 1 (better) mu is multiplied by 1.05; when it is above 1.04 (worse) mu is multiplied by 0.7, the step is rejected and the momentum is reset; otherwise nothing changes. It is asymmetric: grow slowly when things improve, brake hard when they worsen. Results (computed by program): with initial mu0 of 0.02 plain descent needs 411 steps and the adaptive rule 61; with mu0 of 0.12 plain descent blows up while the adaptive rule converges in 95 steps in all, 12 of them rejected; mu0 of 0.08 is already near the best, 100 steps against 93, hardly better."),
    ("Rule table (ratio < 1: mu x 1.05; ratio > 1.04: mu x 0.7; else unchanged) and bars of steps for mu0 = 0.02, 0.12, 0.08: plain 411, blows up, 100; adaptive 61, 95, 93.",) * 2)
add(8, ("quickprop", "quickprop"),
    ("quickprop 用兩次斜率估拋物線的谷底，w₂ 的第 2 步一跳就落在 0", "quickprop estimates the parabola's floor from two slopes, so w₂ lands on 0 at step 2"),
    ("自適應學習率讓 μ 自己調。能不能直接估出谷底的位置？", "The adaptive learning rate lets μ adjust itself. Can we estimate the position of the floor directly?"),
    ("這一頁介紹 quickprop：把每個權重當成各自獨立，用最近兩次的斜率估出拋物線的谷底，直接跳過去。公式：Δw(t) 等於 α(t) 乘 Δw(t 減 1)，α(t) 等於 g(t) 除以 (g(t 減 1) 減 g(t)) 與 α 上限 1.75 取較小者。例子 w2：第 1 步普通步 1 到 負 0.6，斜率 20 變成 負 12；α 等於 負 12 除以 (20 加 12) 等於 負 0.375，Δ 等於 負 0.375 乘 負 1.6 等於 正 0.6，第 2 步剛好落在 0（程式計算）。",
     "This page introduces quickprop: treat every weight as independent, estimate the parabola's floor from the last two slopes and jump straight there. The formula: delta w at t equals alpha at t times delta w at t minus 1, where alpha at t is the smaller of g at t over g at t minus 1 minus g at t, and the cap 1.75. In the example for w2, step 1 is a plain step from 1 to minus 0.6 and the slope goes from 20 to minus 12; alpha equals minus 12 over 20 plus 12, which is minus 0.375, and delta equals minus 0.375 times minus 1.6, which is plus 0.6, so step 2 lands exactly on 0 (computed by program)."),
    ("Parabola J = 10 w2^2 with two slopes 20 at w2 = 1 and -12 at w2 = -0.6; alpha = -12/(20+12) = -0.375, delta = +0.6, so step 2 lands on w2 = 0.",) * 2)
add(9, ("五種做法", "Five methods"),
    ("五種做法需 411、61、100、28、5 步，quickprop 最少；牛頓法一步到原點但要反轉 Hessian", "Five methods need 411, 61, 100, 28 and 5 steps; Newton takes one step but needs a Hessian"),
    ("quickprop 用兩次斜率估拋物線的谷底，w₂ 一跳就落在 0。和其他做法比，步數差多少？", "quickprop estimates the parabola's floor from two slopes and w₂ lands on 0. How do the steps compare with the other methods?"),
    ("這一頁比較五種做法所需步數（程式計算）：普通 μ 等於 0.02 是 411，自適應 61，普通 μ 等於 0.08 是 100，動量 28，quickprop 5。但這個例子每個切面剛好是拋物線，最合 quickprop；真實代價不是二次的，加速都要付出複雜度。延伸：牛頓法用曲率資訊（Hessian 矩陣 H，二階偏導數組成）直接算出谷底，Δw 等於 負 H 的反矩陣乘 g，二次函數一步就到；本例 H 等於 diag(1, 20)，Δw 等於 負 w，一步到原點，代價是要算、存、反轉 Hessian。quickprop 可看成每個權重各做一維牛頓法。",
     "This page compares the steps of five methods (computed by program): plain at mu 0.02 needs 411, adaptive 61, plain at mu 0.08 needs 100, momentum 28 and quickprop 5. But here every slice is exactly a parabola, which suits quickprop best; real costs are not quadratic, and every speed-up costs complexity. Extension: Newton's method uses curvature (the Hessian matrix H of second derivatives) to compute the floor directly, delta w equals minus H inverse times g, and a quadratic needs one step; here H equals diag(1, 20), delta w equals minus w and one step reaches the origin, at the price of computing, storing and inverting the Hessian. quickprop can be seen as a one-dimensional Newton step per weight."),
    ("Horizontal bars of steps: plain mu 0.02 411, adaptive 61, plain mu 0.08 100, momentum 28, quickprop 5; Newton's method: delta w = -H^-1 g, H = diag(1,20), one step to the origin.",) * 2)
add(10, ("小練習", "Exercises"),
    ("兩題小練習：g = (−3.1936, −12)；Δw(3) = (0.5473, 0.96)，w = (−2.6463, 0.36)", "Two exercises: g = (−3.1936, −12); Δw(3) = (0.5473, 0.96) and w = (−2.6463, 0.36)"),
    ("五種做法的步數為 411、61、100、28、5，牛頓法一步到原點。用動量式再算一步，答案是多少？", "The five methods need 411, 61, 100, 28 and 5 steps and Newton takes one. What does the momentum formula give for one more step?"),
    ("兩題小練習，同一個谷底，μ 等於 0.08、α 等於 0.6，第 2 步後 w 等於 (負 3.1936, 負 0.6)，第 2 步更新量 (0.4864, 0)。題 1：梯度 g 等於 (w1, 20 w2) 等於 (負 3.1936, 20 乘 負 0.6) 等於 (負 3.1936, 負 12)。題 2：Δw(3) 等於 0.6 乘 (0.4864, 0) 減 0.08 乘 (負 3.1936, 負 12) 等於 (0.29184 加 0.25549, 0.96) 等於 (0.5473, 0.96)；w 等於 (負 3.1936 加 0.5473, 負 0.6 加 0.96) 等於 (負 2.6463, 0.36)。核對：第 2 步 w2 沒有動，這一步 w2 的慣性是 0，梯度那份 0.96 全成了位移（程式計算）。",
     "Two exercises on the same valley with mu 0.08 and alpha 0.6; after step 2, w equals (minus 3.1936, minus 0.6) and the step-2 update is (0.4864, 0). Q1: the gradient g equals (w1, 20 w2), which is (minus 3.1936, 20 times minus 0.6), equal to (minus 3.1936, minus 12). Q2: delta w at 3 equals 0.6 times (0.4864, 0) minus 0.08 times (minus 3.1936, minus 12), equal to (0.29184 plus 0.25549, 0.96), which is (0.5473, 0.96); w equals (minus 3.1936 plus 0.5473, minus 0.6 plus 0.96), equal to (minus 2.6463, 0.36). Check: w2 did not move in step 2, so its inertia is 0 and the whole 0.96 from the gradient becomes displacement (computed by program)."),
    ("Exercise 1: g = (-3.1936, -12). Exercise 2: delta w(3) = 0.6 x (0.4864, 0) - 0.08 x (-3.1936, -12) = (0.5473, 0.96), w = (-2.6463, 0.36).",) * 2)
PAGES = P
